{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1142422-spirit-soulforging-and-other-thoughts","id":1142422,"title":"Spirit, Soulforging and other thoughts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-09-20T22:54:55-07:00","id":1142422,"title":"Spirit, Soulforging and other thoughts","content":"How would you handle Spirit abilities that allow awakening and communication with spirits when dealing with soul-forged items (eg Oboli). Yes, I know the Dark Umbra is difficult to visit and yes, I know that the wraiths in soulforged objects are meant to be no longer coherent. (Although it's kept darkly ambiguous whether this is true in WtO.) <br /> <br /> My reading of the spirit sphere (and its equivalent, DS) is that it is biased towards the Middle Umbra.(In that Mind,Life and Entropy are additionally necessary for travel to the High or Dark umbrae.) Similary, it feels to me that while multiple POV can be used to explain other sphere effects, Spirit is strongly tied to an animistic worldview. Perhaps this is a layover from it being the &quot;Dreamspeakers&quot; sphere.<br /> <br /> All thoughts and input greatly appreciated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13778-cerulean-scream","name":"Cerulean Scream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13778_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T23:55:35-07:00","id":1142429,"title":"","content":"Where do you want to get<br /> <br /> &quot;Speaking&quot; with spirits/souls bound inside objects? And how to portait it?<br /> I'm not sure I understand what you want to achieve.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12609-lastlostboy","name":"lastlostboy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12609_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T03:10:11-07:00","id":1142445,"title":"","content":"Oh, specifically, can a Mage with DS/Spirit 2 communicate with wraiths that have been changed through soulforging (IF there is a wraith consciousness still there)?<br /> Can a Mage with DS/Spirit 3, awaken a wraith in a relic/artifact in the Dark Umbra. (I'm using the terms &quot;Relic&quot; and &quot;Artifact&quot; as they are used in WtO, not MtA.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13778-cerulean-scream","name":"Cerulean Scream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13778_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T06:24:24-07:00","id":1142479,"title":"","content":"To the best of my knowledge it's never been established how Mages interact with soulsteel or white jade, so you are free to determine how and if it works. Unless there is a really compelling case (such as the mind really is gone, and you've covered how that might not be the case) I assume Mage's can do something, the only difficulty is in figuring out how.<br /> <br /> That said, I don't think animism has much to do with this since we aren't talking about the spirit of a physical object.. If Spirit is involved it is because the object, like everything else in the High, Low, and Middle Umbras, is made of spiritual ephemera. The real issue is contacting a wraith that's been driven into deep dormancy, and likely has a badly damaged mind. Simply awakening that mind with Spirit 3 or a combination of Spirit and Mind could work, but it might take higher levels of one of those spheres if there's significant damage to repair.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T13:47:45-07:00","id":1142680,"title":"","content":"Mostly agree with Ramnesis.<br /> <br /> In theory the Spirit sphere can do all the spirit-ish stuff in whichever vidare (High, Middle, or Low Umbra) that you chose when you got the sphere, but I proposed a &quot;Death&quot; sphere that adds on to Low-Umbra-Spirit based on the Wraith setting:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1140145-proposing-a-death-sphere\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1140145-proposing-a-death-sphere\"> Proposing a Death Sphere - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1140145-proposing-a-death-sphere\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1140145-proposing-a-death-sphere </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Many folks feel that the spheres as presented do a poor job of enabling &amp;quot;necromancy&amp;quot; as they envision it. if they want to raise a corpse, they need Life </div> </div> </div> <br /> <br /> To my mind, awakening an obolus or other chunk of soulsteel would be Death 3, which you could also use to change their form back into a wraith's typical shape. You'd have varying levels of memory and function in the resulting wraith, depending on whether they got soulforged two minutes ago or if you pulled a brick out from an ancient tower in Stygia, and you'd need Mind to either repair the broken consciousness or extract memories from it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7356-haldir2012","name":"haldir2012","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-22T00:21:54-07:00","id":1142822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haldir2012</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1142422-spirit-soulforging-and-other-thoughts?p=1142680#post1142680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mostly agree with Ramnesis.<br /> <br /> In theory the Spirit sphere can do all the spirit-ish stuff in whichever vidare (High, Middle, or Low Umbra) that you chose when you got the sphere, but I proposed a &quot;Death&quot; sphere that adds on to Low-Umbra-Spirit based on the Wraith setting:<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I read your Death sphere before starting this thread, and think it's great. I may well introduce it into my game, however, currently I'm curious as to what people think is possible as presented by the RAW.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13778-cerulean-scream","name":"Cerulean Scream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13778_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-22T00:34:49-07:00","id":1142823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cerulean Scream</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1142422-spirit-soulforging-and-other-thoughts?p=1142445#post1142445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, specifically, can a Mage with DS/Spirit 2 communicate with wraiths that have been changed through soulforging (IF there is a wraith consciousness still there)?<br /> Can a Mage with DS/Spirit 3, awaken a wraith in a relic/artifact in the Dark Umbra. (I'm using the terms &quot;Relic&quot; and &quot;Artifact&quot; as they are used in WtO, not MtA.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the spirit sphere fits more on whole/sane spirits.<br /> Spirit in the umbra is the equivalent of matter/life/forces in the real world. You can say it's the pattern sphere.<br /> <br /> Imagine you have a sleeping madman. You can wake him with life. But to decipher his babble you need mind.<br /> I think with a soulbound/fragmented spirit it's nothing otherwise. You can rouse it with spirit but if you want to gather information you need a mind part in that effect.<br /> <br /> On the other hand: you can sure cure a madman (temporary) with life if your belief is scientific enough (believing in brain chemistry) so I guess you can do the same with spirit. But it would be way harder without mind. And I think every soulbound... erm, well - soul is in a way <i>altered </i>by the forging.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12609-lastlostboy","name":"lastlostboy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12609_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-22T17:18:49-07:00","id":1143088,"title":"","content":"I think there is a definite question about how much of the original intellect survives being soulforged. Maybe mages can talk to oboli, but after you do it once, you don't want to again. How much fun is it to talk to what's effectively a lobotomy victim who is effectively always in the middle of electroshock therapy? And there's not just much left to talk to to.... the sense of self is gone. I bet it's pretty damn near impossible to even get the name of the wraith out of an obolus. And that's for the ones that weren't Drones to begin with. <br /> <br /> There might be more of an issue talking to victims of Moliate. There is at least a process of recovery built in. No matter how bad it is to be a seat cushion, you can be massaged back into human form. Hells, maybe there are Renegades or Heretics running around &quot;freeing&quot; all the moliated cushions by pummeling them so they take so much damage they go into a Harrowing and pop back up at their greatest Fetter? (I can imagine the Harrowing of a cushion....)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}